# Copy to `contracts/.env`. Foundry loads it automatically.
#
# These are the official PUBLIC endpoints from the Monad docs — not secrets, so
# they ship as working defaults. Swap in a private/rate-limited provider before
# mainnet (see the monskills `tooling-and-infra` skill for the provider list);
# public RPCs rate-limit, and that surfaces as a "failed" distribution.
MONAD_TESTNET_RPC_URL=https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz
MONAD_MAINNET_RPC_URL=https://rpc.monad.xyz

# Chain IDs (protocol facts, not config): testnet = 10143, mainnet = 143
# Testnet faucet: https://testnet.monad.xyz

# --- Signing ---
# There is deliberately NO PRIVATE_KEY here, and there must never be one.
# Use an encrypted keystore instead, so the key never sits in a file, in shell
# history, or in this repo:
#
#   cast wallet import monad-deployer --interactive
#   forge script ... --account monad-deployer
#
# `Multisend` has no owner or admin, so the deployer holds no privileged power
# over it — an EOA is acceptable for this contract. `DistributionFactory` (owner,
# fee, pause) must deploy via Safe multisig per CLAUDE.md and the monskills
# `wallet` skill.
